@@ Matrix element wise binary operation
@@ ( A B operation -- AB )
@@
@@ AB[i, j] = A[i, j] operation B[i, j].
@@
@@ DB48X does not provide this for matrices.
@@ It does for 1 dimensional arrays.
«
	→ A B operation
	«
		@@ Create AB.
		A Size 0 ConstantArray
		
		@@ Do it row by row.
		1  A Size Head
		For i
			@@ ( ... -- { i } )
			{} i +
			@@ Get that row from A.
			@@ ( { i } -- { i } A[i, *] )
			A over Get
			@@ Get that row from B.
			@@ ( { i } A[i, *] --  { i } A[i, *] B[i, *] )
			B 3 Pick Get
			@@ (  { i } A[i, *] B[i, *] --
			operation
			@@ Keep the result.
			@@ ( { i } <A[i, *] B[i, *] operation> -- )
			Put
		Next
	»
»
